{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322195-overwhelming-maybe-questions-about-d-tf-crossover","id":1322195,"title":"Overwhelming(maybe) questions about D:tF crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-04T04:26:28-07:00","id":1322195,"title":"Overwhelming(maybe) questions about D:tF crossover","content":"Uh my friend had some questions about D:tF, and he asked me for help.<br /> <br /> 1. Are there any rules about summoning a demon?<br /> 2. Are there any rules about summoning an angel?<br /> 3. Are there any rules about restoring a demon to angel?<br /> 4. What will happen if an angel appears on Earth and does something quite obvious?<br /> <br /> The fourth question has a background. One less-known archmage will restore a demon to/bind an angel, then use it to fight against another very powerful, evil and known being(Maflean Incarna, or Antes). At last he may kill him completely.<br /> <br /> JUST my own answers:<br /> <br /> 1. this resembles summoning a spirit, Spirit 4 at least. But it may add more.<br /> 2. An epic mission. It's up to ST.<br /> 3. Like the 2. . But that rote undoing curse of Caine may be a reference.<br /> 4. Maybe it will make this mage very known and cause a big shock to all splats, and becomes a sign of ToJ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-04-2019, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T05:58:13-07:00","id":1322207,"title":"","content":"1. While there aren't any actual rules, and thus it's left to ST discretion, The Infinite Tapestry suggests that in the case an ST desires to incorporate the setting of Demon when a mage summons a particular demon, there's no reason for the mage to <i>not </i>be summoning the demon from Hell. <br /> <br /> Which implies that it would be, indeed, similar. At least no other method it's proposed, and no reason to treat the spiritual form of a Demon as <i>not</i> spiritual in nature. Thus, yeah, I would say Spirit 4<br /> <br /> Another interesting Sphere it's Prime. Demon Apocalipic forms - the form that manifests in the circle - are at least partially made of Faith (which it's kinda Quintessence). Entropy could be justified to interact with Hell, since Hell it's very related to Oblivion and the depts of the Underworld<br /> <br /> Note that this is something normal humans can do. It shouldn't be hard to contact a Demon, the universe it's geared to make it possible. Magick, however, could be used to impose some of the rules of Mage rather than to merely make the demon appear. Like, say, to make the protection circle actually protect the summoner rather than merely protect the Demon.<br /> <br /> 2. No, it's up to the ST. Among other things becuase we don't know what Heaven is or where it's located. And we don't know what happened to the Angels or why they are missing (or perceived by the demons as missing).<br /> <br /> If the angel it's on Earth like the ones from ToJ, then they are spiritual creatures with a body composed of Faith. So, I would say Correspondence 4 added to Prime and Spirit (at least Prime 3 and Spirit 2)<br /> <br /> 3. Nop, it could be as impossible or easy as the ST wants. <br /> <br /> Personally I don't think that the rote undoing the Curse of Caine should be taken as example because the state of being a Demon it's heavily related to Torment, and Torment isn't a Curse from God (or the Archangels), but rather the <i>rejection </i>of God. It's not an external force imposed on your pattern, but rather a very <i>personal</i> state. All a Mage could do it's to help the Demon understand and face his Torment better...<br /> <br /> ...or completely overhaul the Demon's True Name transforming the creature not only into something else, but also into <i>someone</i> else (which, yeah, would be quite epic. And invasive).<br /> <br /> 4. Wasn't there a supplement with rather epic and evident fight between Lucifer and Belial where Lucifer appeared as an angel to thouzands of spectators?. I think that what happened there has your answer. Humans (under the influence of Technocrats/Camarilla) will call it mass hallucination and not speak of it again. It would be seen by splats as a sign of ToJ. If the mage doesn't figure, his involvement doesn't need to be known. Otherwise the Technocracy hates him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T09:20:16-07:00","id":1322231,"title":"","content":"1: Summoning as telling them to show up or summoning as in making them appear? Both of which are easily done with Spirit. Spirit 2 is all you need to call/yell/politely ask a being to you and Spirit 3 is what you need to get them to manifest, and this is where things get kinda /fucky/.<br /> DTF says Demons don't really have a body so Spirit 3 prob doesn't work on them, but that being said if you made some sort of seal using correspondence you could probably keep the demon bound in its spiritual-ish form while in the circle.<br /> Whether or not the Demons from DTF are 'super special demons' and not the regular demons the Hermetics have been summoning and categorizing for years are left up to the ST, but I like to imagine a bit of overlap. Some of the 'demons' listed by Hermetics? Actually trickster spirits and other malevolent ones. Others? Actual demons as well. (M20 goes on a long spiel about how a spirit can look different to 4 different people so this can be supported by lore)<br /> Spirit 4 does the Spirit 2 thing but forces them to appear, which may make them kinda mad.<br /> <br /> 2: <br /> Hermetics have been summoning angels for as long as they have demons, and the High Umbra has a ton of them. Whether or not the angels are 'super special angels' from DTF depends on the ST I guess, but really are there powers all that different? Perhaps they don't have all the powers they would have in their specific Umbral/High Umbra realm but they are still 'angels' in a sense and could probably do all the things you could ask of a regular angel.<br /> <br /> 3:<br /> These sorts of things are usually personal journeys but I think the idea of saying 'No never' is kinda bad taste, atleast for mage. It mentions the Euthanatos don't fuck with Wraiths because their oblivion is a personal endeavor but high enough level magick should be able to just help a Wraith get over the whole shadow thing. (And could probably just revive their ass to begin with if you can find the other half of their soul thats fucking around), and I think the same for Demon.<br /> Demon should be harder though as they kinda, precede most regular and conventional reality. Maybe it would require lots of study, new or old depending if they are actually the demons that have been getting summoned or new entirely.<br /> It would be hard to help a being out that you basically haven't known existed except for the past few years. Vampires have been around for ages and only masters can even turn the things into Revenants and even that is hard as fuck. (I forget where that Rote is)<br /> <br /> In short: Yeah but its probably hard, the higher the Torment and the unwillingness of the Demon also probably make this harder if not impossible.<br /> <br /> 4: Probably the same thing that happens when a Demon does, it barely works and if it does people forget about it.<br /> Even though Angels may have big boy GOD on their side, Consensus and the general population still doesn't really believe in them as much as they did back sense creation. (Excluding the Lucifer Angel battle thingy but thats just plot shittery and the developers having their super cool OC [Do not steal] Fight infront of the PCs)<br /> <br /> If God wants to be fucking overt and break the consensus his ass can show up himself and do it.<br /> <br /> &quot;One less-known archmage will restore a demon to/bind an angel, then use it to fight against another very powerful, evil and known being(Maflean Incarna, or Antes). At last he may kill him completely.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean this with 100% politeness, but this plot is just crazy as fuck enough for me to think it makes a great plot. Arch-Mages are crazy stupid/silly sometimes and this is so many levels redundant to work.<br /> Unless the Archmage has been doing some /serious/ research, and what better way to get forbidden knowledge than pacts with more demons (And what better way to get fucked in the long run/have your rituals fail), there are so many areas where this might fuck up but it sounds solid/something an Archmage could do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T09:40:01-07:00","id":1322236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 4 does the Spirit 2 thing but forces them to appear, which may make them kinda mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truly Spirit 2 could be enough in certain scenarios, but note that if the Demon it's in Hell it may <i>need </i>to be forced in order to appear...Demons aren't in Hell because they like it, they are trapped there and are forced back there when they haven't a body. It may well be they can't go to you even if they can hear you with Spirit 2, and even if they could they can't stay. You need some way to tether them to the physical realm for the winds of Abyss to not send them back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T09:59:55-07:00","id":1322238,"title":"","content":"I think I hinted enough at that with the whole &quot;You prob need a circle/binding to keep them from being tugged away&quot;, yes.<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 probably works well for the 'weaker' demons who are able to possess bodies and what not/roam around while in their semi-spirit form (Even though they don't have much time) but they probably make it apparent they need a vessel rather quick.<br /> <br /> Spirit 4 probably gets the big ones.<br /> <br /> Both probably need a circle/binding to keep them from being dragged away, for their own benefit of course...and not the fact I'm about to do some serious evil shit to this demonic soul and want him on the other side of this protection barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T10:08:19-07:00","id":1322240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322195-overwhelming-maybe-questions-about-d-tf-crossover#post1322195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. What will happen if an angel appears on Earth and does something quite obvious?<br /> <br /> The fourth question has a background. One less-known archmage will restore a demon to/bind an angel, then use it to fight against another very powerful, evil and known being(Maflean Incarna, or Antes). At last he may kill him completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking from the perspective of a D: TF fan, I don't think this would be possible, at least not without severe repercussions.<br /> <br /> In the beginning, God ordered the Celestial Host to conceal itself from humanity and to let us learn for ourselves the secrets of the Tellurian. Lucifer and the other rebels disobeyed this order and approached humanity. For this, they were denounced and attainted by God. When the loyal angels won the war and sent the demons into the Abyss, God sent down the Flood to wipe away all evidence of supernatural existence. When the Fallen began filtering from the Abyss, they could find no signs of angels or God anywhere in all of Creation.<br /> Presumably, the remaining angels have followed God's orders and have worked to conceal themselves from mankind. An Archmage summoning an angel and using him in an overt display to fight the summoner's enemies would directly countermand an order from God and might either be impossible or prompt celestial retaliation.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is only if you follow Demon's Lore. I don't know as much about Mage's setting but, from what little I know, God might not even exist.<br /> <br /> Also, you should check out Time of Judgement page 90 which details how Angels work gameplay-wise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T10:27:07-07:00","id":1322242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322195-overwhelming-maybe-questions-about-d-tf-crossover#post1322195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Are there any rules about summoning a demon?<br /> 2. Are there any rules about summoning an angel?</div> </div> </div> </div>should be the same than with spirits, as long as you have their true name (easier to find a fallen's true name than an angel's of course)<br /> <br /> and, mages are still technically human, so they can use the summoning/binding rituals from Devil's Due without magic.<br /> I'm not sure if this one works on angels, it might work on angels who were present during creation<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. What will happen if an angel appears on Earth and does something quite obvious? </div> </div> </div>if Yahweh's still around, the angel will end up joining the Fallen club <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> if it's dead, the angel should be fine but will still be hella mad about the whole binding thing (make sure the mage can handle the clash of wills (they probably can't), otherwise your friend can say bye bye to their mage)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T21:48:07-07:00","id":1322557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322195-overwhelming-maybe-questions-about-d-tf-crossover?p=1322240#post1322240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking from the perspective of a D: TF fan, I don't think this would be possible, at least not without severe repercussions.<br /> <br /> In the beginning, God ordered the Celestial Host to conceal itself from humanity and to let us learn for ourselves the secrets of the Tellurian. Lucifer and the other rebels disobeyed this order and approached humanity. For this, they were denounced and attainted by God. When the loyal angels won the war and sent the demons into the Abyss, God sent down the Flood to wipe away all evidence of supernatural existence. When the Fallen began filtering from the Abyss, they could find no signs of angels or God anywhere in all of Creation.<br /> Presumably, the remaining angels have followed God's orders and have worked to conceal themselves from mankind. An Archmage summoning an angel and using him in an overt display to fight the summoner's enemies would directly countermand an order from God and might either be impossible or prompt celestial retaliation.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is only if you follow Demon's Lore. I don't know as much about Mage's setting but, from what little I know, God might not even exist.<br /> <br /> Also, you should check out Time of Judgement page 90 which details how Angels work gameplay-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Existence of The God in Mage is detable. I recall some claims avatars, mage's powerbase, are fragments of the One, which is considered as the god. And some describe mage's magick as &quot;God's power&quot;.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm not familiar with D:tF. I review Angel rule in ToJ. It's all about angels' traits. Of course angels are all Badass and legenary, which makes them may only appear in truly epic story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}